message: "If you use BDR v1.1.0, please cite this software release and the associated scientific preprint where appropriate."
title: "Banco de Dados Resolutivo (BDR) / Resolutive Database Engine"
version: "1.1.0"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Matos"
    given-names: "Marcelo Roldão"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6075-4680"
repository-code: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/resolutive-DB"
url: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/resolutive-DB/releases/tag/v1.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22130421"
abstract: >-
  BDR v1.1.0 extends the stable v1 line with an additive atomic logical-write
  path for Memoria.ia integration. It preserves the existing bdr::Database
  source contract and BDR3/BDW3 readers while adding bdr::AtomicDatabase,
  atomic write_batch/put_many/erase_many operations, explicit durability modes,
  and the versioned BDW4 write-ahead log with all-or-nothing crash recovery.
  Performance claims remain workload-specific and the project does not claim
  strict worst-case O(1) complexity for the complete engine.
keywords:
